Bellwether (formerly pasture): a desktop-pet overlay for Claude Code sessions
MIT licence; see LICENSE.

Bellwether is inspired by desktopPet and its eSheep, and plays desktopPet's pet format.

THIRD-PARTY FORMATS, CODE AND ASSETS
====================================

desktopPet (Adrianotiger/desktopPet), MIT licence
  https://github.com/Adrianotiger/desktopPet
  bellwether's player reads desktopPet's pet format (animations.xml and its schema,
  Resources/animations.xsd). The format and schema are used as a reference, with
  attribution, as the project's README asks ("Please retain attribution ... in any
  redistributed version"). No desktopPet code is copied into bellwether.

Pet art (the sprite sheets inside each animations.xml): NOT included
  The art is NOT committed to this repository and NOT bundled into any build.
  `bellwether pets fetch` downloads it on each user's machine into data/pets/
  (gitignored) from desktopPet at the pinned commit
  1ba33bebed993439f03e502b37e9bd2daf061773, checked against the sha256 in
  pets.lock.json.
  The art's licence is unclear: the repository's MIT licence plainly covers code, not
  obviously the art. The default pet, esheep64, credits "sprites from LiL_Stenly"; the
  original eSheep is by Tatsutoshi Nomura for Fuji Television. Because of that, this
  project does not redistribute the art: each user fetches it from its upstream source
  for their own use. Clearly licensed replacement art is planned.

web-esheep (Adrianotiger/web-esheep), GPL-3.0: NOT vendored
  https://github.com/Adrianotiger/web-esheep
  Used only as a behavioural reference for how the pet XML is interpreted. None of its
  code (esheep.js) is vendored, bundled or copied; bellwether's player
  (shell/src/player/) was written from the desktopPet schema and wiki. Vendoring
  esheep.js would make the shell a GPL-3.0 derivative.

cjpais/Handy, MIT licence
  Consulted as a reference for the wlr-layer-shell initialisation order (the planned
  Linux build). No code copied.

gtk-layer-shell (system C library), LGPL-3.0: not used yet
  The planned Linux build will link the system's gtk-layer-shell dynamically, through
  its Rust binding (MIT). Nothing LGPL is in the macOS build.

DEPENDENCIES
============

Brain (Node): no dependencies at all; Node's built-ins only.

Shell (Rust/Tauri): the crates in shell/src-tauri/Cargo.lock, almost all MIT and/or
Apache-2.0. A few use other permissive licences (Unicode-3.0, Zlib, BSD-3-Clause,
Unlicense, 0BSD), and five are MPL-2.0 (cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short,
option-ext, selectors). Those are linked unmodified, which MPL-2.0 permits without
opening bellwether's own source. Every crate, version and licence is listed in
THIRD-PARTY.md, generated offline by `node scripts/third-party.mjs`.

Shell (npm): one devDependency, @tauri-apps/cli (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), used only to
bundle a .app; it is not part of what runs.

Tauri and wry: Apache-2.0 OR MIT. tao: Apache-2.0 (as its Cargo.toml states).
